From 4422f27fd90be22963eef40fc9936954d8e09087 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:53:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] e-ink: a sleep screen, shown in one step

With debug.sysui.eink_palette (and debug.sysui.eink_sleep, default on):
- SystemUI covers the always-on display with EinkSleepScreen: the time in
  large numerals, the date, the icons of waiting notifications and the
  battery level, black on white (white on black in the dark theme). It
  appears complete when dozing starts, is redrawn from the doze time tick
  and disappears when dozing ends. Nothing animates.
- PhoneWindowManager sets vendor.xrz.hibreak_sleep when the phone starts
  going to sleep or waking up, before the keyguard hears of it, so that
  SurfaceFlinger (frameworks/native EinkMotion) can hold the panel until
  the screen has settled. The panel then goes from the app to the sleep
  screen in one clean refresh, instead of showing the lock screen, the
  doze transition and the always-on layout one after another.

Change-Id: I4f7cbb5d4c84095495d144a38f74c2f7a9ff8f41
